Fri Nov 13 23:08:22 UTC 2026 - Caio César Ortega <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add mowitz-center-on-parent.patch: MwCenter() (alert, list,
  input, file selector and Siag form dialogs) centred dialogs on the
  root window, which on a multi-monitor desktop spans every monitor,
  so "Save?" and friends opened on the wrong screen. Dialogs are now
  centred over the parent application window when it is mapped
  (falling back to the screen centre) and kept inside the screen

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 19:06:19 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add mowitz-selection-utf8.patch: MwSelectionToLatin1() and
  MwLatin1ToUtf8() convert selection text between UTF-8 and the
  Latin-1 Mowitz works in (punctuation outside Latin-1 such as curly
  quotes, dashes and ellipsis is approximated); STRING replies that
  are valid UTF-8 are decoded too, since many clients send UTF-8
  there. MwTextField pastes UTF8_STRING first and offers it when
  copying, and gives Xt a copy of the selection text instead of its
  own buffer (Xt freed it, then MwTextField freed it again)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 17:11:57 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add mowitz-xft-antialias.patch and build --with-xft: document glyphs
  are drawn antialiased through Xft/FreeType from the same URW Type 1
  files t1lib uses, still one by one at the AFM positions, so layout
  and printing are unchanged (MW_NO_XFT=1 brings back the t1lib
  bitmaps). Also load the font before T1_GetFontBBox, which returned
  an empty box (zero line height) until something had drawn with it

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 16:53:20 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- mowitz-xim-latin1.patch: share the input context with XawM through
  a quark-based XContext; in the C locale take composed Latin-1
  letters from the keysym (XwcLookupString returns no characters)
- Add mowitz-filesel-utf8.patch: the file selector showed UTF-8 file
  names as Latin-1 ("relatÃ³rio") and created files with Latin-1
  names; convert between the two at the file system boundary. Also
  size realpath() buffers to PATH_MAX
- Add mowitz-cursor-resource.patch: cursor resource for MwTable and
  MwRichtext

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 15:52:40 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add mowitz-xim-latin1.patch: Mowitz keeps text in ISO 8859-1, but
  XmbLookupString returns UTF-8 in today's locales, so Richtext
  dropped accented letters and TextField stored UTF-8 bytes. New
  MwLookupLatin1()/MwInputInit() give each widget an input context
  on one shared XIM, filter dead keys and return Latin-1

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 14:29:28 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add mowitz-64bit-colors.patch: c.red * 0xffff overflowed int and
  was sign-extended into unsigned long, so white and other bright
  colours were allocated nearly black (black Siag cells on 64-bit)
- Add mowitz-urw-t1lib.patch and build --with-t1lib: text is laid out
  with the Adobe AFM widths, but the X core fonts on Leap have no
  scalable Times/Helvetica at 72 dpi, so glyphs fell back to "fixed"
  and overlapped; render with t1lib using the metric-compatible URW
  fonts from ghostscript-fonts-std instead (FontDataBase, T1= names,
  t1lib.config search path); fix T1_Get_no_fonts -> T1_GetNoFonts
- Mowitz-data requires ghostscript-fonts-std
- Drop the empty NEWS file from the docs

